>> title: Pomegranate Molasses
>> category: Sauces & Gravies
>> tags: pomegranate, middle eastern, syrup, reduction, pantry
>> counters: Shawarma Counter
>> aka: pomegranate molasses, pomegranate syrup, dibs rumman, rub el rumman, narsharab, pomegranate concentrate
>> pairs-with: muhammara, tabbouleh
>> servings: 24
>> time: 1 hr 45 min

>> step: bring the juice up in a wide pan
Bring @unsweetened pomegranate juice{4%cups}(950 mL; 100% juice, nothing from concentrate with sugar in it) up to a bare simmer in a wide #saucepan{}.

>> step: stir in the sugar and lemon
Stir @granulated sugar{1/4%cup}(50 g) and @lemon juice{1%Tbs}(15 mL) into @&(~1)hot juice{} until the sugar has gone.

>> step: reduce 1 hr to a quarter
Reduce @&(~1)sweetened juice{} at a lazy simmer ~simmer{1%hr}, uncovered and stirred now and then, until it is down to about a cup and drags behind the spoon.

>> step: cool 30 min
Cool @&(~1)syrup{} in the pan ~cool{30%min}.
